# Databricks Integration Guidelines

## Authentication Patterns
- Use the unified auth system from `github.com/databricks/databricks-sdk-go/config`
- Implement `PerRPCCredentials` interface for gRPC authentication
- Support both cluster and serverless compute connections
- Handle token refresh automatically through the SDK

## Connection Management
- Use the `DataBricksChannelBuilder` pattern for creating connections
- Support configuration through environment variables or config files
- Implement proper connection cleanup and resource management
- Handle connection errors gracefully with retry logic

## Spark Connect Integration
- Use `github.com/apache/spark-connect-go/v35` for Spark operations
- Follow the session builder pattern for creating Spark sessions
- Implement proper DataFrame operations and transformations
- Handle Spark-specific errors and exceptions

## Error Handling
- Use custom error types for different failure scenarios
- Provide meaningful error messages for debugging
- Implement proper error wrapping with context
- Handle authentication failures separately from connection failures

## Configuration
- Support both cluster ID and serverless configurations
- Use the unified config system for authentication
- Allow runtime configuration changes
- Validate configuration before establishing connections
